{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T20:44:14.732Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"50fbda7191e753d4825499b4","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T20:44:14.732Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The scheduled closeout of merged pull requests fails because delivered Issue items lack the reproduction steps the tracker close policy requires: the closeout derives expected_result from each item's acceptance criteria itself, but repro_steps must already exist on the item. The closeout plan holds three delivered Issue items. Two are genuinely delivered by their merged pull requests; record truthful reproduction steps on each from its own recorded evidence so the next closeout run can close them. The third delivery claim comes from a tracking-only merged pull request against a defect that is still present in the package, so its policy refusal is correct and that item stays open; the separate run-level defect that a single refusal fails the whole closeout run is fixed in pm-github."}],"before_hash":"daceec41cb41229fa57240bde0dc81fcb5600acc1f9559c1ebd49088549e999f","after_hash":"500a1b5e70e1f5d7b1f17ff38ae56ae3ea12e7906c0796a864a32eb31e4f564d","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"02eecd8d8e804d5e12a1d2ebdcf1d50ef05aed80e5b8e57965e08d473ac0ef9d"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T20:44:32.097Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"50fbda7191e753d4825499b4","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T20:44:32.097Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-23T20:44:32.096Z","author":"pi-glm","text":"Class decision finished (scheduled-failure triage 2026-11-23). The closeout dry-run plan holds three delivered Issue items. Two are genuinely delivered: one by the merged pull request that clears the exported NPM_PROJECT_PATH in the continuation fixture, and one by the merged pull request that skips registry-held pending versions and retires stale release candidates. Truthful reproduction steps recorded on each item from its own recorded evidence (the closeout itself derives expected_result from acceptance criteria). The third planned close claims delivery from a tracking-only merged pull request whose acceptance criteria are not met in the current package source, so the completeness-policy refusal is correct and that item stays open; recording reproduction steps on it would grease a false close of a live defect. The run-level defect that a single policy refusal fails the whole closeout and discards every other close is fixed in pm-github (closeout records the refusal and continues). The pm-ops closeout stays red until that fix is released and the caller pin is bumped."}]}],"before_hash":"500a1b5e70e1f5d7b1f17ff38ae56ae3ea12e7906c0796a864a32eb31e4f564d","after_hash":"a558295d82ef35bc75f6c84b53736b5e7929efdb375dade5be5cc75d97570934","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ec15238b123bf4154671d53c3acf405ccc21d24fa7f6a2560a87fbf41cdd6e28"}
